From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:44:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 368/368] tools/asahi: test the gated T8132 cache write-back

Check that the write-back runs only at a firmware-driven suspend, on an
enabled cache, and for T8132 only with apple_mcc.t8132_writeback set
and a boot that can commit (never off arm64); that nothing touches the
cache before that gate; that it writes both apertures to 0, then a
barrier, then polls all four planes; that a plane that does not drain
refuses the sleep and only a finished write-back turns the cache off;
and that the resume turns T8132's cache on through its own enable.
Each check has a mutation that must fail it.

Assisted-by: LLM
